  <ctml:bracket kind="single-elimination">
    <ctml:stage name="title-playoff" order="1">
      <ctml:tie winner="p-fide-409561">
        <ctml:side competitor="p-fide-409561" score="2.5" outcome="win" />
        <ctml:side competitor="p-fide-410608" score="1.5" outcome="loss" />
        <ctml:leg number="1" firstScore="0" secondScore="1" game="g-po1" />
        <ctml:leg number="2" firstScore="1" secondScore="0" game="g-po2" />
        <ctml:leg number="3" firstScore="0.5" secondScore="0.5" game="g-po3" />
        <ctml:leg number="4" firstScore="1" secondScore="0" game="g-po4" />
        <ctml:notes>Title playoff after Gawain Jones and David Howell tied on 7/9. Two rapid games (20+10) were split 1-1, then two blitz games (5+3) went draw and Jones win, so Jones took the playoff 2.5-1.5 and the 2024 British Championship.</ctml:notes>
      </ctml:tie>
    </ctml:stage>
  </ctml:bracket>
  <ctml:notes>British Chess Championship 2024, Championship section: an 86-player, 9-round classical Swiss (40 moves in 90 minutes, followed by 30 minutes to complete the game, plus 30 seconds added per move from move 1) at Hull City Hall, Kingston upon Hull, 27 July - 4 August 2024, organised by the English Chess Federation. Gawain Jones and David Howell tied on 7/9 and Jones won the four-game rapid+blitz playoff 2.5-1.5 to take the title. The source holds 386 records: 379 played Swiss games, 1 double forfeit, 2 byes, and 4 playoff games. The byes (round 1 Madhavan, round 7 Atako) are ctml:nonGame kind="bye-full" rather than games - the source writes them as pseudo-games with Black="bye" and no moves. The double forfeit (round 9, Saunders-Larkin) is an ordinary game with result="0-0" and termination="forfeit": the pairing and both players are known facts, only the play is missing. Its movetext in the source is the literal string "0-0", which is not SAN; the loader tolerates that one shape and nothing else. Scores are computed from the played games plus the byes and asserted to total 381 points. No official final crosstable was available for this build, so tiebreak order is not invented: participant/score is asserted for all 86 players but participant/placement only for the two the playoff decided (1 Jones, 2 Howell). Seed, federation, sex and the event rating come from the official Swiss-Manager starting rank; the PGN carries none of them. The FIDE rating list rolled over mid-event - 42 of the 86 players' Elo tags change on 2024-08-02 (round 7) - so each ratingSnapshot is the July 2024 rating the event started from, the builder asserts every pre-rollover Elo tag matches it, and the August value is recorded in that participant's notes. Player titles come from the starting rank where it gives one, otherwise from the PGN, and the builder refuses to emit if the two contradict each other; seed 79's starting-rank title "AIM" is an arena title outside CTML's PlayerTitleType and the PGN asserts none, so that player is left untitled. The official arbiter list is truncated in the captured source ("FA Igor Doklesti ... All arbiters"), so only the fully-named officials are recorded. ECO codes are classified by longest UCI-prefix match. Identity is by FIDE id. No engine evaluations were present in the source, so none are invented. Uses the CTML 2.1 model (participant/placement, ctml:bracket, ctml:nonGame).</ctml:notes>
  <ctml:source kind="chess.com-pgn">
    <ctml:uri>file:///D:/elysium/sources/twic/2024-british-chess-championship.pgn</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>386 records (379 played Swiss games + 1 double forfeit + 2 byes + 4 playoff games); SHA-256 0d62fa5e9d8401d55f9e8866fe1e8431fa2fd3404cb14f96db393e86743597ee. Moves, clocks, FIDE ids and results authoritative.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
  <ctml:source kind="chess-results-starting-rank">
    <ctml:uri>https://chess-results.com/tnr373174.aspx?lan=1</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>Official Swiss-Manager tournament page (FIDE-Event-ID 373174): starting rank with seed, title, FIDE id, federation, rating and sex for all 86 players, plus organiser, officials, venue, round count and time control. Transcribed to 20240727-20240804_british-chess-championship_starting-rank.tsv; SHA-256 f08dd2364ee4d2fa01e2db6807f8eb11b5c4bb3a2767212bac3f163880d56145.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
